and \"with transform\" runs actually produce different R² before trusting the delta.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"2b5311c4-bff0-4f1c-90e8-8fcd5b453781","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.0.1 — Standing checks from `ADVICE.md` (re-run this pulse-check every week, not just at Week 11)\n\nThese aren't this week's main topic, but skipping them silently is exactly the pattern `ADVICE.md` was written to stop. Answer briefly before treating anything below as a \"win\":\n- Is the CV-leakage question (early-stopping slice overlapping the last walk-forward fold) still deferred? It was deferred once in Week 7 for RF/XGBoost comparability. If LightGBM's baseline this week inherits the same simplification, say so explicitly — don't let it quietly become a fourth week of \"comparable, but not rigorous.\"\n- Do you have even a rough \"would this have made money\" number yet for your current best model? Not required to be exact — a naive PnL-if-every-flagged-signal-was-taken number is enough to keep the actual goal in view.\n- Any target being leaned on as a leaderboard leader — is it still worth re-checking against the volatility-ablation pattern that caught `class_target_3_corrected`?\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"e8540a00-c174-4486-bc1e-789c0fc019c2","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: write 2-4 sentences per bullet above, based on this week's actual state --\n# not a restatement of last week's answer. If nothing has changed, say so explicitly\n# rather than leaving it blank.\nadvice_pulse_check = \"\"\"\nCV leakage status: ...\nRough PnL-if-taken number for current best model: ...\nAny leaderboard leader worth re-ablating: ...\n\"\"\"\nprint(advice_pulse_check)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"3bbb024b-6e31-4a89-8b53-e671f5948df0","cell_type":"markdown","source":"---","metadata":{}},{"id":"b40e30c8-84a2-47a9-bbdc-30392bd9f3b7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.1 — Install packages","metadata":{}},{"id":"91bdd05e-b4f7-42f5-9328-23f753b28113","cell_ty