e raw features directly. The idea is that each level-0 model (LogReg, RF, XGBoost, LightGBM) makes different kinds of mistakes, and a meta-model can learn when to trust which one — this only helps if the level-0 models are meaningfully different from each other, not just differently-tuned versions of the same idea.\n\n**Walk-forward passthrough is the part that's easy to get wrong here:** the meta-model's training rows must be *out-of-fold* predictions from the level-0 models (predictions on data those models didn't see), computed walk-forward, in the same style as `cv_no_scaling()`/`cv_regression()` — not in-sample predictions, which would hand the meta-model a leaked, over-optimistic signal to learn from.","metadata":{}},{"id":"410f5c58-d68d-4fe7-abc1-efd883c90b2c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Level-0 models: LogReg, RF, XGBoost, LightGBM","metadata":{}},{"id":"63cd37ae-b8e5-4207-9666-94e2cfb5f6d3","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: load Week 3/4's tuned LogReg, Week 6's tuned RF, Week 7's tuned XGBoost,\n#       and this week's tuned LightGBM -- one saved model per target/direction, reused\n#       here rather than retrained from scratch.\nlevel0_models = {}\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"ffcc3ca4-7de8-4b91-b801-d21fc353e07d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Level-1 meta-model: LogisticRegression (simple, interpretable)","metadata":{}},{"id":"46f41edc-f736-44bd-affa-5cdcbc1289e0","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: build the out-of-fold prediction matrix (walk-forward, no leakage) for the\n#       level-0 models on one target/direction first, as a single worked example, before\n#       generalizing to all targets.\n# TODO: fit StackingClassifier (or a hand-rolled equivalent using cv_no_scaling-style\n#       walk-forward folds) with LogisticRegression as the final_estimator.\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"00f6400d-d327-440e-be74-8acbc1ea3d5f","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Deliverabl